      ":question/worked-solution": "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} e^{8 x} - x + 2 y e^{4 x}&=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} e^{8 x} + 2 y e^{4 x}&=x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(2 e^{- 4 x})}_{P(x)}y&=\\underbrace{x e^{- 8 x}}_{Q(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=2 e^{- 4 x}$ and $Q(x)=x e^{- 8 x}.$",
